            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of nifedipine (corinfar) on cerebrovascular circulation in patients with exertion-induced stenocardia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headache as a side effect of corinfar treatment courses for angina of effort was more commonly seen in patients with pretreatment dystonic rheoencephalographic changes. A single corinfar dose produced a drop of venous tone. Corinfar-associated headache was less common in patients after long-term treatment with high-dose nitroglycerin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
